(183172, 10265, 327, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/>#95<br/>Hello Waltoml.<br/>This shot fits the challenge. <br/>The light is good. <br/>It''s an interesting object with lots of facets in different sizes.<br/>Of course rust is always a good thing to shoot and looks good here.<br/>Here with your shot I think the view or perspective could of been improved. I''m thinking you were trying to shoot down on the wheel from above. This is okay but the crop left the silver &lt;?&gt; at the bottom. This is a distraction. Is that a wrench? Part of the bike? An error?<br/>I think the focus is fine along with the colors. Maybe they could of been made a bit richer with some level adjustment but they look good to me.<br/>I like the shot. I will say the most detrimental part is the _noise_ in the full image. I''m not too sure why you have this much? Maybe the 100 ISO was just too high here?<br/></td>', 'Critique Club#95Hello Waltoml.This shot fits the challenge. The light is good. It''s an interesting object with lots of facets in different sizes.Of course rust is always a good thing to shoot and looks good here.Here with your shot I think the view or perspective could of been improved. I''m thinking you were trying to shoot down on the wheel from above. This is okay but the crop left the silver <?> at the bottom. This is a distraction. Is that a wrench? Part of the bike? An error?I think the focus is fine along with the colors. Maybe they could of been made a bit richer with some level adjustment but they look good to me.I like the shot. I will say the most detrimental part is the _noise_ in the full image. I''m not too sure why you have this much? Maybe the 100 ISO was just too high here?', '2003-01-06 00:45:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(183179, 10260, 1880, '<td valign="top">JD,<br/> <br/>You have your ribbon!!! Congrats this is a terrific image. Was it as nice in color? Black and White seems to make images much more dramatic.  Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>Bob<br/></td>', 'JD, You have your ribbon!!! Congrats this is a terrific image. Was it as nice in color? Black and White seems to make images much more dramatic.  Keep up the good work. Bob', '2003-01-06 00:47:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(183183, 10188, 714, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a well taken photo.  I like the sepia tone and the way the tracks are setting.</td>', 'Congrats on a well taken photo.  I like the sepia tone and the way the tracks are setting.', '2003-01-06 00:49:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(183190, 10151, 327, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/>#57<br/>Hello there Mzanoni.<br/>Feels like home .....because you travel so much. Road warriors! What a life.<br/>Empty chairs.........lonely!!! SUPER&gt;!<br/>The first thing my eye is drawn to the shadows. That might just be me. I love photos of shadows and this is attractive.<br/>The blue of the seat and the suttle blues in the pillar are very nice. It really sets the mood and feeling of this shot. <br/>I will say the focus is a tad soft......so what? This shot was good and should of scored higher. Like it.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club#57Hello there Mzanoni.Feels like home .....because you travel so much. Road warriors! What a life.Empty chairs.........lonely!!! SUPER>!The first thing my eye is drawn to the shadows. That might just be me. I love photos of shadows and this is attractive.The blue of the seat and the suttle blues in the pillar are very nice. It really sets the mood and feeling of this shot. I will say the focus is a tad soft......so what? This shot was good and should of scored higher. Like it.', '2003-01-06 00:52:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(183194, 10246, 772, '<td valign="top">should have scored much higher....</td>', 'should have scored much higher....', '2003-01-06 00:54:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(183202, 10266, 327, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/>#19<br/>Hello Juhaseila - I loved your portrait shot!! The little girl-!! Just a doll.<br/>Okay the shot at hand. Funny how several of the comments below wanted to be there in your shot. I think you should take that as a very high compliment. I would agree with them, the shot is inviting. <br/>The light is just how it looks. Winter light. Kool. <br/>The color or lack of colors makes this shot feel cold. Perfect.<br/>There is movement of the blowing snow to tie the image together.<br/>Very nice, good focus, action, light. Nice feeling. Nice composition.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique Club#19Hello Juhaseila - I loved your portrait shot!! The little girl-!! Just a doll.Okay the shot at hand. Funny how several of the comments below wanted to be there in your shot. I think you should take that as a very high compliment. I would agree with them, the shot is inviting. The light is just how it looks. Winter light. Kool. The color or lack of colors makes this shot feel cold. Perfect.There is movement of the blowing snow to tie the image together.Very nice, good focus, action, light. Nice feeling. Nice composition. ', '2003-01-06 00:58:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(183205, 10336, 2003, '<td valign="top">Xmas night from a hill in El Segundo, overlooking LAX - took quite a few snaps &amp; elapse - looks like i picked the right one --- the color of the restaurant arches cycle thru a variety of colors, just like the new ''mini-towers'' that mark the entrance to the airport - purple would have looked good, too --- if i had a location with the right view, i could have shot the landing pattern with at least 9 planes ...</td>', 'Xmas night from a hill in El Segundo, overlooking LAX - took quite a few snaps & elapse - looks like i picked the right one --- the color of the restaurant arches cycle thru a variety of colors, just like the new ''mini-towers'' that mark the entrance to the airport - purple would have looked good, too --- if i had a location with the right view, i could have shot the landing pattern with at least 9 planes ...', '2003-01-06 00:59:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(183257, 10255, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>When I first viewed this photograph, I did not really see ''Travel'' in it.  The image itself does not show travel taking place or a mode of travel.  I do see your intent with the photo, but I think, in general, you may have deviated too far from the theme of the challenge to score better with this image.  <br/> <br/>I think a little lower angle possibly would be an improvement so that the information on the computer screen is more visible to the viewer.  With an image like this, however, the viewer will have to spend too much time viewing to really grasp your interpretation of the challenge.  For this reason, I believe that your comments were few and far between.  There is nothing here that grabbed the viewer and said "spend some time looking at me" :)  <br/> <br/>Technically, I don''t see any problems with this image at all.  Subjectively, I think it could have been stronger.<br/> <br/>The technical ability tells me that you can definitely have command of your camera... keep plugging :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) When I first viewed this photograph, I did not really see ''Travel'' in it.  The image itself does not show travel taking place or a mode of travel.  I do see your intent with the photo, but I think, in general, you may have deviated too far from the theme of the challenge to score better with this image.   I think a little lower angle possibly would be an improvement so that the information on the computer screen is more visible to the viewer.  With an image like this, however, the viewer will have to spend too much time viewing to really grasp your interpretation of the challenge.  For this reason, I believe that your comments were few and far between.  There is nothing here that grabbed the viewer and said "spend some time looking at me" :)   Technically, I don''t see any problems with this image at all.  Subjectively, I think it could have been stronger. The technical ability tells me that you can definitely have command of your camera... keep plugging :) John Setzler', '2003-01-06 01:42:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(183261, 10160, 92, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon ! This is a wonderful photo !!!!!!!</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon ! This is a wonderful photo !!!!!!!', '2003-01-06 01:53:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(183321, 10274, 843, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Overall I like this shot very much. Excellent composition and good use of cropping. Black and white was a good choice, as the weather seems a bit dreary. It also adds to the "cold" look of the urban setting. The only negative thing I can see is that it could be slightly sharper. I don''t know what your lighting situation was, but this may have been possible by closing the aperature a little more. I know it''s tough to take a well-exposed picture in the shade with the sky in the background, but you managed to pull it off well.<br/> <br/>Great job!<br/>-greenem2</td>', 'Critique Club Overall I like this shot very much. Excellent composition and good use of cropping. Black and white was a good choice, as the weather seems a bit dreary. It also adds to the "cold" look of the urban setting. The only negative thing I can see is that it could be slightly sharper. I don''t know what your lighting situation was, but this may have been possible by closing the aperature a little more. I know it''s tough to take a well-exposed picture in the shade with the sky in the background, but you managed to pull it off well. Great job!-greenem2', '2003-01-06 04:25:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(183338, 10145, 843, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Very cute and humorous! I love the rich colors and crisp focus. There are a few things IMO that could have made this photo even better. The obvious one is the warning sticker on the seat. If you had time you could have placed some cloth over it perhaps. Also, the whites are blown out due to the flash. This is forgivable since the main focus is on the baby''s face. Lastly, I think this is an instance where one would like the subject dead center. I would have tried to compose it so that the baby was head on and filled the entire frame.<br/> <br/>An overall good job. A few simple adjustments in environment and composition and you''d have a winner in my book.<br/> <br/>-greenem2</td>', 'Critique Club Very cute and humorous! I love the rich colors and crisp focus. There are a few things IMO that could have made this photo even better. The obvious one is the warning sticker on the seat. If you had time you could have placed some cloth over it perhaps. Also, the whites are blown out due to the flash. This is forgivable since the main focus is on the baby''s face. Lastly, I think this is an instance where one would like the subject dead center. I would have tried to compose it so that the baby was head on and filled the entire frame. An overall good job. A few simple adjustments in environment and composition and you''d have a winner in my book. -greenem2', '2003-01-06 04:45:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(183394, 10251, 2170, '<td valign="top">You got ripped off...this was one of my favorites this week!</td>', 'You got ripped off...this was one of my favorites this week!', '2003-01-06 07:28:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(183414, 10235, 472, '<td valign="top">i still am wondering what this is :)</td>', 'i still am wondering what this is :)', '2003-01-06 07:44:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(183415, 10147, 472, '<td valign="top">WOW, Anita!!  Coming up in the world!! And with a 1.3 mpx camera no less :):):)</td>', 'WOW, Anita!!  Coming up in the world!! And with a 1.3 mpx camera no less :):):)', '2003-01-06 07:44:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(183431, 10336, 3087, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts</b> <br/>Great capture of lights in the night  quite interesting subject matter.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content</b> <br/>The position of the tower at the left is balanced by the arches at the right. I like the diagonal lines of the flight taking off  kind of surreal that only the lights and not the craft are captured It feels a little top heavy on the dark area of sky but not hugely so. Point of focus for me is the pair of diagonal lines.<br/> <br/><b>Background</b> <br/>Most of the interest is definitely in the foreground, as intended. I like that I can just make out the hills behind.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work - Technical</b> <br/>Well exposed. No faults that I can see!<br/> <br/><b>Digital Processing - Technical</b> <br/>Seems fine to me!<br/> <br/><b>Fits The Challenge</b> <br/>Most definitely.<br/> <br/><b>Your Opinion On The Photo</b> <br/>One that grew on me as I viewed it second and third times. The content doesnt have a great impact for me but what is there has certainly been composed and captured well.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club   Initial thoughts Great capture of lights in the night  quite interesting subject matter. Composition/ Content The position of the tower at the left is balanced by the arches at the right. I like the diagonal lines of the flight taking off  kind of surreal that only the lights and not the craft are captured It feels a little top heavy on the dark area of sky but not hugely so. Point of focus for me is the pair of diagonal lines. Background Most of the interest is definitely in the foreground, as intended. I like that I can just make out the hills behind. Camera Work - Technical Well exposed. No faults that I can see! Digital Processing - Technical Seems fine to me! Fits The Challenge Most definitely. Your Opinion On The Photo One that grew on me as I viewed it second and third times. The content doesnt have a great impact for me but what is there has certainly been composed and captured well.', '2003-01-06 08:00:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(183439, 10260, 5515, '<td valign="top">Who gave this shot a 1 or a 2????? Had to be someone trying to get the score down. It is a shame people have to be so lame as to do stuff like that. <br/> <br/>Congrats on a great image.... You deserve it...<br/> <br/></td>', 'Who gave this shot a 1 or a 2????? Had to be someone trying to get the score down. It is a shame people have to be so lame as to do stuff like that.  Congrats on a great image.... You deserve it... ', '2003-01-06 08:05:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(183440, 10251, 2954, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who have commented and to those who thought i deserved a better score.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-01-06 08:10:20.</i></td>', 'Thanks to all who have commented and to those who thought i deserved a better score.', '2003-01-06 08:06:03.000000', '2003-01-06 08:10:20.000000', 0),
(183444, 10105, 3087, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts</b> <br/>Excellently captured  vivid colours and strong shapes.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content</b> <br/>The content is certainly exciting  reminds me of childhood (I have family living in Florida so we visited a number of times when I was a kid  and Ive returned a few times as an adult too). The firework itself is just superb  perfectly round  perfectly captured  very strong graphical element. Its position over the castle is excellent, as is the blue lighting on the castle itself. <br/>My main criticism would be the slightly messy feel of the bottom edge of the image. I dont know whether this would best be resolved by cropping more or less at the bottom  depends what else was there  but this crop doesnt add anything to your shot. Cropping at the top is also slightly tight though doesnt detract, in my mind.<br/>Id also prefer to see a larger image size to enable me to better see the detail in the castle itself.<br/> <br/><b>Background</b> <br/>Nicely black (on my monitor anyway). <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work - Technical</b> <br/>Light of castle and firework well captured.<br/> <br/><b>Digital Processing - Technical</b> <br/>Seems fine  cropping is not ideal.<br/> <br/><b>Fits The Challenge</b> <br/>Yes.<br/> <br/><b>Your Opinion On The Photo</b> <br/>Has a WOW factor but the potential is not maximised. Am surprised it didnt rank a little higher however.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club   Initial thoughts Excellently captured  vivid colours and strong shapes. Composition/ Content The content is certainly exciting  reminds me of childhood (I have family living in Florida so we visited a number of times when I was a kid  and Ive returned a few times as an adult too). The firework itself is just superb  perfectly round  perfectly captured  very strong graphical element. Its position over the castle is excellent, as is the blue lighting on the castle itself. My main criticism would be the slightly messy feel of the bottom edge of the image. I dont know whether this would best be resolved by cropping more or less at the bottom  depends what else was there  but this crop doesnt add anything to your shot. Cropping at the top is also slightly tight though doesnt detract, in my mind.Id also prefer to see a larger image size to enable me to better see the detail in the castle itself. Background Nicely black (on my monitor anyway).  Camera Work - Technical Light of castle and firework well captured. Digital Processing - Technical Seems fine  cropping is not ideal. Fits The Challenge Yes. Your Opinion On The Photo Has a WOW factor but the potential is not maximised. Am surprised it didnt rank a little higher however.', '2003-01-06 08:08:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(183448, 10237, 472, '<td valign="top">lol, no, ive seen a pic with 99 ...</td>', 'lol, no, ive seen a pic with 99 ...', '2003-01-06 08:10:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(183452, 10100, 3087, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts</b> <br/>Good colour, interesting content, composition a little static.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content</b> <br/>The content is good  I like the strong colours and the very strong connection to the challenge. The background of sarong and sand is also very appropriate.<br/>For me the composition is a little less satisfactory  I dont have anything against centred compositions but it just seems a little boring in this case. However I do like the way the lines of the passport, book and tickets converge towards the back/ top of the image  it makes the viewpoint a little more interesting.<br/> <br/><b>Background</b> <br/>As above, very appropriate and appealing colours and textures  wouldnt mind a touch more sand.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work - Technical</b> <br/>Looks good to me<br/> <br/><b>Digital Processing - Technical</b> <br/>Ditto<br/> <br/><b>Fits The Challenge</b> <br/>Very much so.<br/> <br/><b>Your Opinion On The Photo</b> <br/>I like the colours and the content but find the composition doesnt feel quite right.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club   Initial thoughts Good colour, interesting content, composition a little static. Composition/ Content The content is good  I like the strong colours and the very strong connection to the challenge. The background of sarong and sand is also very appropriate.For me the composition is a little less satisfactory  I dont have anything against centred compositions but it just seems a little boring in this case. However I do like the way the lines of the passport, book and tickets converge towards the back/ top of the image  it makes the viewpoint a little more interesting. Background As above, very appropriate and appealing colours and textures  wouldnt mind a touch more sand. Camera Work - Technical Looks good to me Digital Processing - Technical Ditto Fits The Challenge Very much so. Your Opinion On The Photo I like the colours and the content but find the composition doesnt feel quite right.', '2003-01-06 08:14:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(183459, 10250, 3087, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>[b[Initial thoughts[/b]<br/>Colourful abstract with interesting background.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content</b> <br/>Have no idea what the content actually is which makes it hard to comment on and very hard to understand connection to challenge theme.<br/>Composition is very centred, though this works well for an abstract of this nature. <br/>Good selection of colours.<br/> <br/><b>Background</b> <br/>I like the texture and colours of the background.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work - Technical</b> <br/>Very hard to judge as not sure what intention was. <br/> <br/><b>Digital Processing - Technical</b> <br/>As above.<br/> <br/><b>Fits The Challenge</b> <br/>Have no idea.<br/> <br/><b>Your Opinion On The Photo</b> <br/>Interesting to look at but since I have little experience in abstract art, difficult for me to make a fair critique on.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club  [b[Initial thoughts[/b]Colourful abstract with interesting background. Composition/ Content Have no idea what the content actually is which makes it hard to comment on and very hard to understand connection to challenge theme.Composition is very centred, though this works well for an abstract of this nature. Good selection of colours. Background I like the texture and colours of the background. Camera Work - Technical Very hard to judge as not sure what intention was.  Digital Processing - Technical As above. Fits The Challenge Have no idea. Your Opinion On The Photo Interesting to look at but since I have little experience in abstract art, difficult for me to make a fair critique on.', '2003-01-06 08:21:12.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(183470, 10289, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Zadore...<br/> <br/>I''m at a bit of a loss on how to really critique this photo.  There is nothing wrong with the image, but there is not a single particularly inspiring element of the photo other than the clouds.  The clouds do look nice, but they aren''t the focus of the challenge unfortunately.  I can''t really see a way to improve this particular image.<br/> <br/>This photo placed mid pack in the challenge, which tells me that the overall voter thought it was just an average photo.  Maybe some stronger ''punch line'' would have improved the performance here on a larger scale.  I think PTLParsons'' comment sums it up best.  <br/> <br/>Keep up the good work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Zadore... I''m at a bit of a loss on how to really critique this photo.  There is nothing wrong with the image, but there is not a single particularly inspiring element of the photo other than the clouds.  The clouds do look nice, but they aren''t the focus of the challenge unfortunately.  I can''t really see a way to improve this particular image. This photo placed mid pack in the challenge, which tells me that the overall voter thought it was just an average photo.  Maybe some stronger ''punch line'' would have improved the performance here on a larger scale.  I think PTLParsons'' comment sums it up best.   Keep up the good work :) John Setzler', '2003-01-06 08:29:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(183487, 10188, 5044, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! A well deserved win. I''m sure glad I stayed away from my train tracks idea. I would not have stood a chance. Enjoy the moment.</td>', 'Congratulations! A well deserved win. I''m sure glad I stayed away from my train tracks idea. I would not have stood a chance. Enjoy the moment.', '2003-01-06 08:50:53.000000', NULL, 0),
